<!DOCTYPE score-partwise PUBLIC "-//Recordare//DTD MusicXML 4.0 Partwise//EN" "http://www.musicxml.org/dtds/partwise.dtd">
<!-- Synthetic (written for this repository): clef changes at the end of measures that are longer than their time
     signature, on a staff of the second instrument (after Vieuxtemps, Violin Concerto No. 4 Op. 31 m194, piano left
     hand, where the measure was taken as shorter than its 12/8). Violin, then piano (2 staves), 4/4.
     m1 and m3 last five quarters in every staff (no time change). m1: after its last note (the last node of the
     measure) the piano left hand changes from bass to treble clef for m2. m3: the left hand changes back to the bass
     clef after its last note, and a second right-hand voice follows in the file. Both clefs belong to the left hand
     (piano staff 2); the right hand keeps its treble clef. -->
